        "enemy_type": "Ancient Scribe",
        "pre_narrative": "The Two-Mark Terror presents a sentence where the colon and semicolon seem equally defensible — but one is clearly more precise. He has corrupted a royal announcement in the Crypts' hall of records. The announcement sets up a specific fact, and the relationship between the clauses must be parsed carefully.",
        "passage": "A royal announcement reads: \"The king has made his decision[underlined: ; the dispute over the northern border will be resolved by the end of the month].\"",
        "question_stem": "In the passage above, which version of the underlined portion is correct?",
        "option_a": "; the dispute over the northern border will be resolved by the end of the month",
